Lint-010
%Warning-UNUSEDSIGNAL: data_mem.v:8:22: Bits of signal are not used: 'addr'[31:10,1:0]
  In instance riscv_core.u_dmem.
Fix: Added valid_word_addr to require a word-aligned byte address in the 1 KiB data window.
  Invalid writes are ignored and invalid reads return zero.

Lint-011
%Warning-UNUSEDSIGNAL: inst_mem.v:4:22: Bits of signal are not used: 'addr'[31:10,1:0]
  In instance riscv_core.u_imem.
Fix: Added a range and alignment check to instruction memory.
  Invalid fetches return the RISC-V NOP encoding (32'h00000013).

Lint-012
%Warning-LATCH: alu.v:18:5: Latch inferred for signal 'riscv_core.u_alu.tmp' (not all control paths of combinational always assign a value)
Fix: Defaulted tmp to 33'd0 at entry to the combinational block.
  Arithmetic cases overwrite it before use, so it needs no storage.

Lint-013
%Warning-LATCH: instr_decode.v:17:5: Latch inferred for signal 'riscv_core.u_dec.opc' (not all control paths of combinational always assign a value)
Fix: Defaulted opc to 7'd0 before the reset branch.
  The normal decode path still assigns instr[6:0].

Lint-014
%Warning-SYNCASYNCNET: riscv_core.v:5:16: Signal flopped as both synchronous and async: 'reset'
  Async use: riscv_core.v:107:12. Sync use: data_mem.v:17:12.
  pc.v also used an asynchronous reset, and reg_file.v used a synchronous reset.
Fix: Changed the PC and MMIO state blocks to posedge clk only.
  Active-high state reset is sampled at a rising edge, matching data memory
  and the register file. The init/elab test now expects a clock-only event.

